# Volla Phone Plinius: the camera's device nodes stay with Android's camera HAL, not with every app
# of the session. systemd's 70-uaccess.rules tags all video4linux and media nodes "uaccess", and on
# a /dev with ACLs (plinius-kernel from 6.1.192-12) 73-seat-late.rules then gives the active user
# rw on each of them: about 50 ISP, sensor and media-controller nodes of MediaTek's drivers.
# No app of the session needs them, the camera reaches apps through the HAL in the container,
# camera-hal-bridge and PipeWire, where the camera permission of each app applies (GNOME Settings >
# Privacy > Camera). Opening the ISP's imgsys node while the HAL uses it even hits a kernel BUG.
# Kept: the video node of the USB webcam gadget (plinius-usb-webcam, under the UDC's gadget), and
# the hardware video decoder and encoder. Those two are also in the group video (their own rules,
# 71-plinius-vcodec.rules and plinius-vdec), which only administrators are in: other local
# accounts reach them through the ACL while they are the active session, not while another account
# is in front of the phone (attack review 2026-11-18, L14). The match is on the node's name, so a
# node without that attribute (media controllers) still loses the tag.
ACTION=="remove", GOTO="plinius_camera_no_uaccess_end"
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTR{name}=="mtk-vcodec-enc|mtk-vcodec-dec", GOTO="plinius_camera_no_uaccess_end"
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux|media", DEVPATH!="*/gadget*", TAG-="uaccess"
LABEL="plinius_camera_no_uaccess_end"
